      "body": [
        {
          "type": "TextualBody",
          "label": "Recto",
          "value": "\n<ol dir=\"ltr\"><li>His servant Yosef b. Ma\u1e25f\u016b\u1e93.</li>\n<li>In (your) na(me), O Mer(ciful One).</li>\n<li>I bless God, to whom greatness belongs, and give thanks to Him with praise and with song, He who is mighty and exalted, great and abundant in His goodness, He who</li>\n<li>cannot be searched out, who sees all and is seen by every living thing, who preceded all creation,</li>\n<li>whose majesty and might are in the heavens. They are great and beyond reckoning. Our lord and the crown of our heads</li>\n<li>will comfort you, my heart, the light of my heart and the light of my eyes, Samuel ha-Nagid, nagid of the treasured people. May God be his help and shield him in His shelter,</li>\n<li>magnify his honor, save him from the violence of the government, bless every work of his hands, bless, guard and help him,</li>\n<li>and exalt the splendor of all his dear ones. Amen. Your excellency&rsquo;s servant, grateful for your bounty and [proclaimer] of some of your virtues,</li>\n<li>informs you of some of what befell me at the hands of Ab\u016b Sa\u02bf\u012bd Ibn Fustuqa,</li>\n<li>about whom your excellency asked me. I approached him and drew near to his high status for three months</li>\n<li>until I obtained for him a rescript (tawq\u012b\u02bf) cancelling his capitation tax (jizya). Then, afterwards, he turned</li>\n<li>the jurist (faq\u012bh<i>)</i> against us, and also our lord the chief judge (q\u0101\u1e0d\u012b al-qu\u1e0d\u0101t), and all the Muslims.</li>\n<li>He paid a dinar to someone in my presence, but (that person) could not fulfill his request. Then he brought</li>\n<li>me into the Islamic legal system (al-shar\u012b\u02bfa) and sued me for the whole amount, and he made me lose the fee of a court messenger, two dirhams.</li>\n<li>Because of how hard he pressed me and complained that I had afflicted them (?) [. . .]</li>\n<li>Then they were the cause of what happened to me with the \u1e24aver Yeshu\u02bfa. He informed against me</li>\n<li>to the tax collectors. He went after me because I had a musallaqa (? or mu\u1e6dallaqa, divorc&eacute;e?), and she had converted to Islam. I came to check on</li>\n<li>my son at her house on Saturday, and they meant to burn me (?). Yet I repaid him with kindness and what was incumbent upon me.</li></ol>\n",
          "format": "text/html"
        }
      ],
      "motivation": [
        "sc:supplementing",
